-- title:
--   Descendant sets are index intervals
-- statement:
--   Let an ordered tree have levels $\{0,\dots,s_k-1\}$ with monotone surjective parent maps, and for levels $i\le j$ let $\mathrm{anc}:\text{level }j\to\text{level }i$ be the ancestor map. For a node $v$ at level $i$, $\mathrm{lo}(v)$ is the index of its first descendant at level $j$ and $\mathrm{hi}(v)$ is one more than the index of its last. Then for every $s$ at level $j$,
--   $$
--   \mathrm{anc}(s)=v\iff\mathrm{lo}(v)\le s<\mathrm{hi}(v) .
--   $$
--
--   The descendants of a node occupy a contiguous block of the lower level.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/Nonexpansive/OrderedTreeIntervals.lean#L58-L83

